sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 89.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the near-onset Turing wavenumber (fastest mode 1.961 µm, classic k_c wavelength 1.946 µm) and replaces the six-e-fold linear horizon with the cubic law d_t u = σ(k) u - γ u³. Activator rms plateaus at 0.258. Peak-to-peak spacing on that stripe field is 1.961 µm (RMSE 0 against the rung, because mode (12, 0) is an exact harmonic of the 12-wavelength domain). The spectral centroid, which includes cubic harmonics, is 1.957 µm and is not identical to the reference. The comparison figure draws the specimen mask. Last-frame CV similarity to the Hanson male is 83.1 (12 frames, 640×480). Overall 89.3/100 (faithfulness 88.6, reproducibility 90.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, pillow 13.0.0, matplotlib 3.11.2. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 995582 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 f5e970f4b35dd2de2e9dfd0cce027d6f4508e22e303456d314dd2a0814dd140a (sha256 f5e970f4b35dd2de2e9dfd0cce027d6f4508e22e303456d314dd2a0814dd140a), spec_fingerprint 965c9feaa244c1d56d6c4a07371f6ea2f5478ae5cc72e76fe09fa1a3b7eec04c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 965c9feaa244c1d56d6c4a07371f6ea2f5478ae5cc72e76fe09fa1a3b7eec04c; artifact_sha256: f5e970f4b35dd2de2e9dfd0cce027d6f4508e22e303456d314dd2a0814dd140a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=19f8aa499fe6bbdd..., datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=8bb7f34ac600cac7..., datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=ff6dbcfc60370723..., datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=4cf8077a656a0c44...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the two-species dispersion relation and the conditions for a diffusion-driven band. | Richards et al. (2005) sequenced D. pseudoobscura. They do not report a Turing wavelength. | Kopp (2011) reviews sex-comb evolution. The two-segment comb is not a 1.961 µm stripe. | The Hanson 2019 Commons file is a lateral photograph of an adult male under CC BY-SA 4.0.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian (0.84, -0.90, 1.55, -1.20) s^-1 and diffusivities D_u = 0.028046, D_v = 0.131825 µm²/s place the fastest mode at 1.961 µm. | Split-step integration of σ(k) u - γ u³ with γ = σ_max / 0.35², 320 steps, seed 3200. A weak x-axis orientation weight is a stand-in for the anterior-posterior axis. | Chronoseries comparison: Δlog10 λ versus planitibia is -2.003 and versus santomea is +1.717, with Δage = 0 Ma. Diffusivity would have to be about 10112 times larger to put this Jacobian on the planitibia rung.; transfer_boundary: 1.961e-6 m is the assigned detail rung of this slot, not a published histological period for a D. pseudoobscura ocellus. | Planitibia and santomea wavelengths are neighbouring MorphoEval primordium rungs, not measurements made in this script.; does_not_claim: That Richards 2005 measured a reaction-diffusion wavelength. | That the sex comb or the third-chromosome inversions are produced by this 2 µm mode. | That planitibia → pseudoobscura → santomea is a stratigraphic ancestor-descendant series. | That spacing RMSE = 0 is an independent empirical discovery. The domain was built so twelve critical wavelengths fit exactly, and the saturated stripes lock to that harmonic. | That the growth GIF is a time-lapse of embryogenesis.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: A published histological period at 2 µm for D. pseudoobscura is still absent. 1.961 µm remains the assigned detail rung.",
            "remediation needed: Pass-1 cubic saturation, peak-to-peak spacing, specimen-mask overlay, and a readable 2 µm inset are in this pass. CV similarity is 83.1." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.893"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (Cursor cloud agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

